      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This paper presents a Fourier analysis of the Ortega equation that examines the growth dynamics of plants, specifically the pollen tubes or non-meristematic zones of elongating coleoptiles. A frequency-induced transition from highly nonlinear (periodical) growth-like the one observed in pollen tubes-to monotonically ascending and asymptotically saturated (sigmoid-like) growth, which is anticipated within the framework of a 'two-fluid model', is shown. A dynamic phase diagram is calculated and presented in the form of a live video clip."},
